Licensing of the material in this repository
============================================

This file DESCRIBES the licence terms the imported material already carries.
It GRANTS NOTHING. CeraLive is not a copyright holder of any patch content here
and is not in a position to license it to anyone.

Read docs/PROVENANCE.md for the full audit, including what we verified, what we
did not, and the open questions. This file is only a summary.


Patch content (upstream/, patches/)
-----------------------------------

Two backports of two mainline Linux kernel commits, taken verbatim from
armbian/linux-rockchip pull request #487 (OPEN, not merged) via
`git format-patch`:

  * 0001  Linux commit f77a066f4ed307db93aafee621e2683c3bda98ce
          "ASoC: hdmi-codec: Allow playback and capture to be disabled"
          Copyright (C) Mark Brown <broonie@kernel.org>
          Reviewed-by: Russell King (Oracle) <rmk+kernel@armlinux.org.uk>

  * 0002  Linux commit e041a2a550582106cba6a7c862c90dfc2ad14492
          "ASoC: hdmi-codec: only startup/shutdown on supported streams"
          Copyright (C) Emil Abildgaard Svendsen <emas@bang-olufsen.dk>
          Applied upstream by Mark Brown <broonie@kernel.org>

  Backported to the Armbian rk-6.1-rkr5.1 BSP branch by
  Stepan Mazurov <smazurov@gmail.com>, who added the bracketed backport
  annotations, the Tested-by, and the second Signed-off-by on each commit.

Both patches modify only files that already exist in the Linux kernel, and both
of those files are plain GPL-2.0-only Linux sources:

  * sound/soc/codecs/hdmi-codec.c    // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
                                     Copyright (C) 2015 Texas Instruments
                                     Incorporated - https://www.ti.com/
                                     Author: Jyri Sarha <jsarha@ti.com>

  * include/sound/hdmi-codec.h       /* SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only */
                                     Copyright (C) 2014 Texas Instruments
                                     Incorporated - https://www.ti.com
                                     Author: Jyri Sarha <jsarha@ti.com>

The series adds NO new file, alters NO SPDX line, and touches NO MODULE_LICENSE
value. There is no dual-licence question here and no MIT branch to elect: this
is GPL-2.0-only Linux kernel code, modified by GPL-2.0-only Linux kernel
patches, redistributed as GPL-2.0-only kernel patches. See docs/PROVENANCE.md.

Both source repositories carry a collection-level licence of their own, unlike
the situation documented in the sibling repo CERALIVE/rk3588-kernel-patches:

  * torvalds/linux            GPL-2.0 (COPYING, with the Linux-syscall-note
                              exception for UAPI headers — not relevant here,
                              since neither patch touches include/uapi/)
  * armbian/linux-rockchip    a Linux kernel fork; same COPYING


